{
  "_doc": {
    "zone": "All local date-times are America/New_York wall-clock ISO strings without an offset (earlier offset on a fall-back ambiguity). Epoch values are milliseconds.",
    "keys": "KEY = RULE ( \"@\" HHMM | \"_h\" H ), RULE = Dn (n >= 0) | W1-4 | Wd1-7 | Wn1-7 | Dom1 | Dom15 | DomL | Mo1-3, HHMM = local wall-clock time rounded to 5 minutes, H = 0-12. Regex: ^(D(0|[1-9]\\d*)|W[1-4]|Wd[1-7]|Wn[1-7]|Dom1|Dom15|DomL|Mo[1-3])(@([01]\\d|2[0-3])[0-5][05]|_h([0-9]|1[0-2]))$ A clock key's D/W/Wd/Wn/Dom/DomL count from its first hit (the first time HHMM comes round at least 60s after the reference time), so D0 is the next HHMM, D1 the one after; Wd is the first hit on that weekday, Wn the second; Mo counts from the reference time's snooze day. Hour offsets count from the reference time's snooze day.",
    "extract": "extractKeys(at, target): keys sorted by code unit; setId = keys joined by \"__\", or null when there are no keys.",
    "quickCredit": "The quick-time slot (HHMM) a commit credits, or null when it credits none: a same-snooze-day commit, or a suggestion whose picked key is an hours offset.",
    "resolve": "resolveKey(key, now) -> epochLocal, or null when it can't resolve more than 60s into the future.",
    "labelDist": "Label day phrase for key resolved at resolvedLocal from now. dist = max(0, snoozeDay(resolved) - calendarDate(now)); weekday = ISO weekday of snoozeDay(resolved); phrase is one of today|tomorrow|inDays|inWeeks|this|next|inTwoWeeks|calendar; family is the key's date-rule family; region (timed keys only) is the time-of-day name of the resolved time.",
    "labelOffset": "Same-day hours-offset label kind: littleWhile for up to 3 hours, muchLater beyond.",
    "quickTimes": "quickTimes(partitions, now): each partition is a wire `tod` map; expect lists the chosen clockMinutes (minutes after local midnight) in clock order. Picked greedily with the same discount as rankDeep, by clock distance around midnight.",
    "rank": "rank(partitions, now): each partition is a wire partition; expectKeys are the chosen rows' keys in row (time) order.",
    "wire": "fromWire(raw) must equal normalized, and toWire(fromWire(raw)) must equal normalized. picks keeps only keys 1..20 or none with a positive integer count. A raw partition without v >= 2 was saved before clock keys counted from their first hit: each set's clock keys are resolved the old way (date rule counted from the snooze day of its t) and, if they agree on one target, the set is re-extracted from (t, target) keeping c and t; sets that land on one id merge (both decayed to the later t, summed). toWire always writes v: 2.",
    "rankDeep": "rankDeep(partitions, now): the first 20 distinct rows in greedy selection order (a row's 1-based index is its rank). After each pick every other key's score drops by the pick's score x 2^(-|minutes apart| / 30), floored at 0; the floor still applies to the undiscounted score, and equal discounted scores go to the higher undiscounted one. Keys spent because they land at the same time as a winner take no index. expectShownKeys are the menu's rows: the first 5, in time order.",
    "pickLog": "pickLogKey(rankDeep(partitions, now), target): the 1-based rank of the deep row whose time is target's minute, however it was picked, or none when no row is."
  },
